    "result_text": "Done. The build passes and the one test (`AcceptanceTest`, the full suite) is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe stored `telephone` is already canonicalized to E.164 (by the existing create-owner pipeline). I added a derived, read-only `telephoneDisplay` that formats it for humans, reusing the country-code knowledge that already lived in `OwnerTelephones`.\n\n1. **`OwnerTelephones.java`** \u2014 added a public `toDisplay(String)` that splits the E.164 number into its country calling code (via the existing `NATIONAL_DIGITS` codes, longest-match) and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. A number with an unrecognized code or non-E.164 input is returned unchanged. The class was made `public` (mirroring the sibling `OwnerIdentities`, which the mapper already uses the same way); `toE164`/`hasValidNationalLength` stay package-private.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", ...)` plus a small `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` default that delegates to `OwnerTelephones.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`, consistent with the other derived-field helpers. Raw `telephone` still maps through unchanged.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nFormatting logic stays in the telephone unit that owns country-code knowledge; the mapper only wires it in \u2014 no duplicated string handling and no new dependency.",
